<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.5.2: Adding Two Equations in a System</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00442</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.5.2: Adding Two Equations in a System</md:title>
    <md:uuid>7ea12b2f-6a7f-4b72-b7f0-f7e8ab6d3d95</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>A teacher purchased 20 calculators and 10 measuring tapes for her class and paid $495. Later, she realized that she didn’t order enough supplies. She placed another order of 8 of the same calculator and 1 of the same measuring tape and paid $178.50. </para>
<para><figure><media alt="A calculator and a tape measure"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/eb59aa995bdee5256748462eafd7d4ea1d9bd853"/></media></figure></para>
<para>This system represents the constraints in this situation. Discuss questions 1 – 4 with a partner, then answer the questions.</para>
<para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{c}20c+10m=495\\8c+m=178.50\end{array}\right.\)</para>

<!--Q#1-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> In this situation, what do the solutions to the first equation mean? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para><b>Answer:</b></para>
    <para>The solutions to \(20c+10m=495\) are all possible combinations of unit prices for the two items that make a total of $495 when buying 20 calculators and 10 measuring tapes.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q#2-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> What do the solutions to the second equation mean? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para><b>Answer:</b></para>
    <para>The solutions to \(8c+m=178.50\) are all possible combinations of unit prices for the two items that make a total of $178.50 when buying 8 calculators and 1 measuring tape.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q#3-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> For each equation, how many possible solutions are there? Explain how you know. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para><b>Answer:</b></para>
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
    <para>In the first equation, \(c=20\) and \(m=9.50\) would make the equation true, as would \(c=15\) and \(m=19.50\).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q#4-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> In this situation, what does the solution to the system mean? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para><b>Answer:</b></para>
    <para>The price for a calculator and the price for a measuring tape that would make both equations true (or satisfy both constraints).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="32dc415c-799a-45eb-b3d5-2ea77595b854" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q#5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="affa2239-f309-4373-acb5-e69e5d2a8610" data-problem-comparator="float" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="21.50">
    <problem>
      <para>Find the value of \(c\). </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
    </problem>
    <para><b>Answer:</b></para>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 21.50</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q#6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="f69535b1-f2b8-4130-8515-37f3538969ca" data-problem-comparator="float" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="6.50">
    <problem>
      <para> Find the value of \(m\).</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
    </problem>
    <para><b>Answer:</b></para>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 6.50</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
